# Upstream files this integration deliberately does not ship.
#
# Intentionally empty.
#
# This used to list twenty-five files: sixteen marketing pages under
# resources/js/pages/public/ plus layouts/PublicLayout.jsx, public/assets/js/main.js
# and the same seven shell components dental drops. Those render this eye centre's
# own public face. They were deleted because eye is a module inside TibaDesk rather
# than a product with its own front door, and their router — the SPA's own — could
# bring a second website back with nothing in the overlay to stop it.
#
# They are now shipped and routed nowhere. resources/js/components/App.jsx is the
# overlay's own, and it redirects / to the panel and imports no public page and no
# PublicLayout, so all twenty-five are unreachable. They stay in the tree so eye
# can still be diffed against bestvision and so the marketing content is not lost.
#
# The rule is upstream files are never deleted: a module that drops its author's
# files cannot be diffed back against the source it came from, and "that page is
# gone" is not a thing you want to discover after the fact. What keeps a second
# website off the screen is routing, not deletion.
#
# If you ever need a path deleted here, list it one per line below. Paths are
# relative to the application root and are checked by bin/sync-apps.sh --verify.
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
